<spell-notebook "table theming">
	<header level="1">
		Table
		<header>A table displays a collection of data grouped into rows.</>
	</>
	<table-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-table-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (`:root` included), on the
			table itself (it's in your page) or through `::part(scroller)`. The sheet reads each through a private alias, so
			nothing blocks them. The shadow root's only piece is the `scroller` part.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-table {
			  --ui-table-header-background: var(--ui-surface);
			  --ui-table-striped-background: oklch(from var(--ui-primary) l c h / 0.06);
			}
			ui-table::part(scroller) {
			  scrollbar-gutter: stable;
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				`inverted` swaps in its own `--ui-table-inverted-*` colours, and `padding` (`compact`, `md` ...) replaces the cell padding
				with their own steps (`--ui-table-padded`, `--ui-table-compact-padding-*`). `--ui-table-stack-by: container`
				makes every table in a region stack by its own width;  `--ui-table-stack-by: none`, never. Never set the `--_ui-*` names: they're the sheet's private
				plumbing.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-table" playground>
				<ui-table celled>
					<ui-row header>
						<ui-cell>Name</>
						<ui-cell>Status</>
						<ui-cell>Notes</>
					</>
					<ui-row>
						<ui-cell>John</>
						<ui-cell>Approved</>
						<ui-cell>None</>
					</>
					<ui-row>
						<ui-cell>Jamie</>
						<ui-cell>Approved</>
						<ui-cell>Requires call</>
					</>
					<ui-row>
						<ui-cell>Jill</>
						<ui-cell>Denied</>
						<ui-cell>None</>
					</>
					<ui-row footer>
						<ui-cell header>3 People</>
						<ui-cell header>2 Approved</>
						<ui-cell></>
					</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
